  </tbody>
</table>

<p>Per-request waste came out <code class="inl">[11, 12, 4]</code>, all under the
<code class="inl">bs − 1 = 15</code> bound. The middle request holds 900 tokens and
<code class="inl">900 % 16 = 4</code>, so its tail block is partial by 12.</p>

<h2><span class="n">04</span>Part 2 — the gather</h2>

<p>At this point I had a page table with no MMU. <code class="inl">translate()</code>
would tell you where a token lived, and then nothing went and got it. Attention needs an
actual <code class="inl">(T, d)</code> matrix — <b>T</b> rows for T tokens of history,
<b>d</b> numbers per row — where row <em>i</em> holds the vector for logical position
<em>i</em>, whichever physical block it happens to sit in.</p>

